{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c9ec7209435144b9c4411f7c3814d765fafe29e84552b345e9a171ca468d916e","digest":{"component_or_area":"DC renderer (wiki_render.py)","key_entities":["adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py","_convert function","subprocess.Popen","start_new_session=True","rebar._proc.reap_process_group","pypandoc-binary==1.15","reconciler.dc_pandoc_timeout_s","NOTICE file","pyproject.toml","_config_schema.py","_config_sources.py","REBAR_RECONCILER_DC_PANDOC_TIMEOUT_S","tests/golden/config_surface.json","docs/config.md"],"problem_keywords":["pandoc timeout","process group reaping","subprocess robustness","DC renderer","pathological input hang","GPL compliance","license provenance"],"propositions":["Pandoc subprocess invocations can hang indefinitely without a caller-side wall-clock timeout, as observed with a corpus body spinning at 95.8% CPU for 13.5 minutes","subprocess.run(timeout=) only reaps the direct child process, allowing grandchild processes to survive and continue consuming resources after timeout","The pypandoc-binary wheel bundling pandoc 3.6.1 (GPL licensed) lacks provenance recording in the repository","Rendered output must remain byte-identical to the landed per-unit renderer when replacing subprocess.run with owned Popen + process group reaping","The dc_pandoc_timeout_s configuration value must be reachable from config file, environment variables, and documented in the standard four-file config surface","The pandoc binary pin in pyproject.toml must be verified in CI to prevent silent version drift"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":